{"Title":"An Act relative to the police cadet program in the city of Brockton","BillNumber":"H4630","DocketNumber":"HD4882","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"MMD1","Name":"Michelle M. DuBois","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/MMD1","ResponseDate":"2024-02-06T14:32:37.727"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"MMD1","Name":"Michelle M. DuBois","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/MMD1","ResponseDate":"2024-02-06T14:32:37.7266667"},{"Id":"RAM1","Name":"Rita A. Mendes","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/RAM1","ResponseDate":"2024-02-06T14:32:37.7266667"}],"JointSponsor":{"Id":"RAM1","Name":"Rita A. Mendes","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/RAM1","ResponseDate":"2024-02-06T14:32:37.727"},"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/H4630/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Bill","Pinslip":"By Representatives DuBois of Brockton and Mendes of Brockton, a petition (subject to Joint Rule 12) of Michelle M. DuBois and Rita A. Mendes (with the approval of the mayor and city council) relative to the police cadet program in the city of Brockton.  Public Service.  [Local Approval Received.]","DocumentText":"\tSECTION 1.(a) Notwithstanding chapter 31 of the General Laws, any person who has completed not less than 2 years of service as a police cadet in the police department of the city of Brockton under the provisions of section 21A of chapter 147 of the General Laws may be appointed, by the Mayor, to fill a vacancy in a position in the lowest grade in the police force of the city without certification from an eligible list prepared under the provisions of said chapter 31. Such appointment may only be made of a person who (i) is on a police entrance eligible list prepared under said chapter or (ii) passes a qualifying examination to be given by the state division of personnel administration.\r\n\t(b) The appointment shall be subject to a program established by the mayor of the city and approval by the personnel administrator of the state division of personnel administration and the municipal police training committee. The program shall include provisions for recruitment of applicants for appointment as police cadets in the city of Brockton and for appointment from an eligible list prepared after a competitive examination administered under the supervision of Mayor or designee for the city of Brockton.\r\n\t(c) A person appointed to the regular police force of the city of Brockton under this act shall, after satisfactory completion of the probationary period, be deemed to be permanently appointed to said police force and subject to said chapter 31.\r\n\tSECTION 2. If any federal or state administrative or court order requires the listing of city of Brockton police candidates on separate groups, each group to be listed according to the law of the commonwealth, then this act shall be subject to such listing.\r\n\tSECTION 3. Not more than 33 1/3 per cent of the total number of appointments to the regular police force of the city of Brockton in any calendar year shall be made under the provisions of this act. The appointing authority of the city of Brockton shall report in writing to the personnel administrator in said division of personnel administration any appointment made under the provisions of this act.\r\n\tSECTION 4. The provisions of section 61 of chapter 31 of the General Laws shall apply to appointments made under this act.\r\n\tSECTIONS. This act shall take effect upon its passage.\r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Suspend Rules","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"H33","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/H33"},"Votes":[]},{"Action":"Favorable","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J23","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J23"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[]}